// the projection now stores those tiles out of the accumulators the fp32 C
// came from, so the same float is narrowed once either way. `narrow ctx` read
// the fp32 context and narrowed it; the attention kernel already divided by
// the softmax denominator in fp32 registers, so again the same float reaches
// fp16 by a shorter road. Anything but equality here would mean one of those
// two claims is wrong.
//
// Both are compared where their own output is still visible -- the packed v
// plane and the fp16 A operand -- rather than only through the block's
// output, which is stage 4b's rule and the reason that test found what it
// found. The block output is compared too, and is likewise identical.
func TestGPUBlockFusedLayout(t *testing.T) {
